.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt SSL_STREAM_RESET 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm SSL_stream_reset
.Nd reset a QUIC stream
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ssl.h
.Ft typedef struct ssl_stream_reset_args_st {
     uint64_t quic_error_code;
 } SSL_STREAM_RESET_ARGS;

 int
.Fo SSL_stream_reset
.Fa "SSL *ssl"
.Fa "const SSL_STREAM_RESET_ARGS *args"
.Fa "size_t args_len"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn SSL_stream_reset
function resets the send part of a QUIC stream when called on a QUIC
stream SSL object, or on a QUIC connection SSL object with a default
stream attached.
.Pp
If
.Fa args
is non-NULL,
.Fa args_len
must be set to
.Qo Li sizeof(*args) Qc .
.Pp
.Em quic_error_code
is an application-specified error code, which must be in the range [0,
2**62-1]. If
.Fa args
is NULL, a value of 0 is used.
.Pp
Resetting a stream indicates to an application that the sending part of
the stream is terminating abnormally.
When a stream is reset, the implementation does not guarantee that any
data already passed to
.Xr SSL_write 3
will be received by the peer, and data already passed to
.Xr SSL_write 3
but not yet transmitted may or may not be discarded.
As such, you should only reset a stream when the information transmitted
on the stream no longer matters, for example due to an error condition.
.Pp
This function cannot be called on a unidirectional stream initiated by
the peer, as only the sending side of a stream can initiate a stream
reset.
.Pp
It is also possible to trigger a stream reset by calling
.Xr SSL_free 3 ;
see the documentation for
.Xr SSL_free 3
for details.
.Pp
The receiving part of the stream (for bidirectional streams) continues
to function normally.
.Sh NOTES
This function corresponds to the QUIC
.Sy RESET_STREAM
frame.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Returns 1 on success and 0 on failure.
.Pp
This function fails if called on a QUIC connection SSL object without a
default stream attached, or on a non-QUIC SSL object.
.Pp
After the first call to this function succeeds for a given stream,
subsequent calls succeed but are ignored.
The application error code used is that passed to the first successful
call to this function.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr SSL_free 3
.Sh HISTORY
.Fn SSL_stream_reset
was added in OpenSSL 3.2.
